WEBVTT

00:00.810 --> 00:03.350
U-Um, Takada-kun...

00:03.620 --> 00:04.490
Here.

00:06.230 --> 00:10.120
I found a four-leaf clover, so I 
made it into a good luck charm.

00:10.530 --> 00:13.640
This way you won't get hurt anymore.

00:14.280 --> 00:16.000
You're giving it to me?

00:16.610 --> 00:18.070
Thanks!

00:22.450 --> 00:24.540
I wouldn't take that, Takada.

00:24.540 --> 00:27.320
A good luck charm from the Grim Reaper?

00:27.320 --> 00:29.540
Are you sure it's not cursed?

00:29.540 --> 00:33.490
Huh? Four-leaf clovers bring you good luck!

00:33.490 --> 00:35.000
Doesn't matter!

00:35.000 --> 00:39.050
Anything made by the Grim Reaper 
turns into a cursed item!

00:39.050 --> 00:41.400
You're gonna end up being cursed!

00:41.840 --> 00:43.180
Woo-hoo!

00:43.180 --> 00:45.050
Thanks, Nishimura-san!

00:45.050 --> 00:46.850
Wait, were you even listening?

00:46.850 --> 00:50.610
Well, cursed items are 
really rare, aren't they?

00:50.610 --> 00:53.300
I've never seen one in stores!

00:53.300 --> 00:54.610
Well, duh!

00:54.870 --> 00:58.910
There's no way anyone would sell 
something the Grim Reaper made!

00:59.670 --> 01:01.310
Guess you're right!

01:01.800 --> 01:07.530
A good luck charm made by Nishimura-san 
is one of a kind!

01:08.240 --> 01:11.200
So I'm super stoked!

01:11.200 --> 01:12.660
Y-Yeah...

01:12.980 --> 01:15.950
Will I get cursed if I hold on to it forever?

01:15.950 --> 01:17.910
It'll be my treasure!

01:18.510 --> 01:20.340
Th-Thanks...

01:21.630 --> 01:24.220
I'm the one who should be saying thanks.

02:50.980 --> 02:55.020
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

02:57.570 --> 03:03.030
<i>Episode 10 "My First Time Having Guests Over"</i>

03:00.520 --> 03:02.560
Oh, no! our eyes met!

03:02.560 --> 03:03.880
How chilling.

03:08.370 --> 03:10.450
What's wrong, Nishimura-san?

03:10.450 --> 03:11.650
Nothing much.

03:12.000 --> 03:15.840
Some of the girls are saying that it's 
bad luck to make eye contact with me.

03:15.840 --> 03:18.050
Whoa, that's awesome!

03:18.050 --> 03:18.850
Huh?

03:19.150 --> 03:21.250
They must mean you have Mystic Eyes!

03:21.250 --> 03:23.100
That's amazing, Nishimura-san!

03:23.100 --> 03:26.320
Huh? Sure, okay.

03:26.320 --> 03:28.110
M-Mystic Eyes?

03:28.390 --> 03:31.920
It's an ability you need to gaze 
into the boundaries of our world!

03:31.920 --> 03:34.220
The curse is really a side effect

03:34.220 --> 03:36.350
and not the true essence of Mystic Eyes!

03:36.670 --> 03:39.850
I-It's nothing as neat as that.

03:40.630 --> 03:44.250
They're just having a laugh
and going on about

03:44.250 --> 03:48.880
my glaring, cold, creepy eyes...

03:48.880 --> 03:50.930
I totally get it.

03:50.930 --> 03:51.870
What?

03:51.870 --> 03:53.920
They're really pretty!

03:53.920 --> 03:59.230
You do have big, cool, mysterious eyes.

04:00.260 --> 04:01.880
Class Journal

04:00.680 --> 04:01.890
N-No way!

04:02.100 --> 04:06.880
And you know, I go on about you
all the time when I'm with you!

04:06.880 --> 04:10.570
It's always so much fun that I wind up
having a good laugh, too.

04:10.570 --> 04:15.710
Your eyes are so amazing and pretty, 
I could stare into them all day!

04:16.840 --> 04:19.440
Wh-What's the matter, Nishimura-san?!

04:20.160 --> 04:21.900
Is it your Mystic Eyes?

04:21.900 --> 04:23.860
Are your Mystic Eyes throbbing?!

04:24.570 --> 04:27.570
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

04:33.150 --> 04:35.480
G-Good morning.

04:35.750 --> 04:38.800
What's the story of bandage on your eye?!

04:38.800 --> 04:39.750
Ew!

04:39.750 --> 04:40.750
Look at that!

04:41.000 --> 04:43.140
Trying a little too hard, huh?

04:43.140 --> 04:46.660
She wants to get Takada-kun's 
attention that badly?

04:46.660 --> 04:47.920
Hmm?

04:49.770 --> 04:51.930
You did this for me?

04:51.930 --> 04:53.770
Thanks, Nishimura-san!

04:54.640 --> 04:56.450
N-No, I didn't!

04:56.450 --> 04:59.770
I just happen to have a bump on my eyelid.

04:59.770 --> 05:01.230
Huh, really?

05:01.230 --> 05:02.270
Are you okay?

05:03.350 --> 05:05.740
She's obviously lying!

05:06.020 --> 05:10.280
She definitely put on that bandage just 
to get attention from Takada-kun!

05:10.280 --> 05:12.550
So there's nothing wrong with your eye?

05:12.550 --> 05:13.700
That's a relief!

05:13.700 --> 05:15.310
Sh-She's wrong.

05:15.310 --> 05:18.600
It's nearly healed,
but it's not all the way there yet.

05:18.600 --> 05:20.970
Why not just take off the bandage, then?

05:20.970 --> 05:23.330
If it's almost healed, it'll be fine!

05:24.200 --> 05:25.550
Okay.

05:42.180 --> 05:43.720
I-I took it off.

05:43.720 --> 05:44.820
Just like you wanted.

05:46.570 --> 05:48.820
Nishimura-san, you look pretty...

05:52.600 --> 05:54.820
You look pretty healed up now!

05:54.820 --> 05:56.820
Th-That's what you meant!

05:56.820 --> 05:58.330
Thanks.

06:00.330 --> 06:02.590
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

06:06.410 --> 06:08.270
Hey, hey, check it out.

06:08.270 --> 06:12.040
Get a load of that white coat
Nishimura's wearing.

06:12.360 --> 06:14.690
Not that it can hide the fact
that she's the Grim Reaper.

06:14.690 --> 06:16.040
Right?

06:19.210 --> 06:22.750
<i>I'm having fun at school now.</i>

06:24.960 --> 06:26.150
How lame.

06:26.600 --> 06:28.570
Right? She totally is.

06:28.930 --> 06:30.810
I meant you girls.

06:31.190 --> 06:33.050
Huh, did you say something?

06:33.050 --> 06:35.450
What's wrong, Kasahara-san?

06:37.520 --> 06:38.470
<i>No...</i>

06:39.560 --> 06:44.370
<i>Nishimura-san's trying pretty hard for once.</i>

06:47.190 --> 06:50.930
<i>The lamest one of all... is me.</i>

06:53.280 --> 06:56.390
You're pretty cool, Kasahara-san.

06:56.390 --> 06:57.250
Huh?

06:58.290 --> 06:59.770
What's with that look?!

06:59.770 --> 07:02.060
Did I say something weird?

07:02.060 --> 07:05.430
No, you're just so...

07:05.430 --> 07:06.170
What?

07:06.170 --> 07:07.670
Well, never mind that.

07:07.670 --> 07:10.380
What do you think is so cool about me?

07:10.380 --> 07:13.420
What? Your clothes, for one thing...

07:13.800 --> 07:14.880
My clothes, huh?

07:15.470 --> 07:17.410
Like the way you dress!

07:17.730 --> 07:20.460
Oh, and you run really fast.

07:20.710 --> 07:23.280
<i>She thinks I'm cool? No way.</i>

07:24.100 --> 07:28.800
<i>Even though I made fun
of her clothes back then...</i>

07:29.370 --> 07:32.870
U-Um, Kasahara-san?

07:34.890 --> 07:38.790
You really throw me off, you know that?

07:41.440 --> 07:43.900
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

07:44.750 --> 07:47.660
Last night was the worst!

07:47.660 --> 07:50.490
I had a dream about the Grim Reaper!

07:50.490 --> 07:51.720
No kidding?

07:51.720 --> 07:53.160
Does that mean you're cursed?

07:53.160 --> 07:55.720
Maybe she's stealing your soul!

07:57.820 --> 07:59.620
Nishimura-san!

07:59.620 --> 08:01.150
Hey, listen to this!

08:01.410 --> 08:04.370
Last night, I had a dream about you!

08:04.370 --> 08:07.100
Thanks for visiting me in my sleep!

08:07.370 --> 08:10.600
Well, I didn't really...

08:11.130 --> 08:15.130
You think the power of the Grim 
Reaper's curse will make me stronger?

08:15.130 --> 08:16.080
Beats me.

08:16.530 --> 08:19.660
Maybe I've already received your power!

08:19.660 --> 08:21.050
Jeez...

08:21.730 --> 08:22.980
Didn't you know?

08:22.980 --> 08:27.150
If you appear in someone's dreams,
that means they've been granted a curse!

08:27.150 --> 08:29.580
Y-Yeah, I've heard that.

08:29.980 --> 08:33.820
You're the only one who'd be happy about it.

08:33.820 --> 08:35.730
Huh, you think so?

08:36.050 --> 08:40.650
When I show up in people's dreams, 
everyone says that it's creepy.

08:40.880 --> 08:42.940
Huh, is that so?

08:43.580 --> 08:45.810
Oh, but not <i>everyone</i>!

08:46.530 --> 08:49.780
There's one person right here who's glad!

08:49.780 --> 08:52.790
I'd never say something like that!

08:54.690 --> 08:59.840
Everyone else might be scared,
 but I <i>want</i> to be cursed!

08:59.840 --> 09:03.810
You're... plenty strong without curses.

09:03.810 --> 09:05.430
Huh? How so?

09:05.720 --> 09:08.960
I recently saw you
in a dream, too, Nishimura-san.

09:08.960 --> 09:10.440
Wait, really?!

09:10.680 --> 09:12.470
You were there, too, Takada.

09:12.470 --> 09:15.730
For real?! That makes me so happy!

09:15.730 --> 09:18.220
Nishimura-san, it was 
the two of us together!

09:18.220 --> 09:19.960
I-I get it already!

09:19.960 --> 09:21.860
Attaboy, Hino-kun!

09:23.690 --> 09:26.710
<i>Those tank tops look good on you two...</i>

09:23.830 --> 09:26.710
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

09:27.130 --> 09:29.550
I'm sorry, Nishimura-san.

09:29.550 --> 09:32.030
Taiyou has lessons today.

09:32.030 --> 09:34.040
Thank you very much.

09:34.040 --> 09:36.460
He should be back pretty soon.

09:36.460 --> 09:41.170
You really shouldn't have. I'm just 
here to return some of his manga.

09:41.390 --> 09:44.050
He's into all that edgy middle
schooler stuff, right?

09:44.050 --> 09:46.440
You don't have to force yourself to read that.

09:46.440 --> 09:48.170
Oh, no, that's not...

09:48.850 --> 09:50.300
<i>Edgy...?</i>

09:50.300 --> 09:54.640
Nishimura-san, do you get teased 
for hanging out with him?

09:54.640 --> 09:55.280
What?

09:55.280 --> 09:57.460
You know, boys can be so stupid.

09:57.460 --> 10:00.990
Whenever they see a boy and girl together,
they'll go, "Look! They're a couple!"

10:01.230 --> 10:04.420
So I was worried my brother's
putting you in a tight spot.

10:04.420 --> 10:07.210
No way! Nothing of the sort.

10:07.210 --> 10:09.430
Oh? Wait, are you totally down with that?

10:09.430 --> 10:11.080
No, well...

10:11.470 --> 10:16.940
I'm fine being teased, because Takada-kun 
always comes to save the day.

10:19.180 --> 10:20.620
I'm home!

10:20.620 --> 10:22.800
Well, speak of the devil, Nishimura-san!

10:22.800 --> 10:25.130
Your future husband is here!

10:25.130 --> 10:26.420
Yukiko-san!

10:26.420 --> 10:28.720
D-Don't tease me like that!

10:29.070 --> 10:30.980
What's this?

10:30.980 --> 10:35.020
Didn't you say you were fine being teased?

10:35.020 --> 10:36.940
W-Well...

10:38.730 --> 10:41.590
Hey, you came over, Nishimura-san!

10:41.590 --> 10:42.870
What's wrong?

10:42.870 --> 10:43.990
What do you mean?

10:43.990 --> 10:45.900
Well, I'm saying...

10:45.900 --> 10:48.300
I'm sorry, Nishimura-san!

10:48.300 --> 10:52.260
You're so adorable that I couldn't 
help myself from picking on you!

10:53.390 --> 10:55.040
P-Picking on her?

10:55.040 --> 10:59.820
You may be my sister, but I won't 
let you hurt Nishimura-san!

10:59.820 --> 11:00.670
What?!

11:00.670 --> 11:03.440
You two are just so adorable!

11:03.440 --> 11:04.650
What do you mean?!

11:05.010 --> 11:10.020
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

11:11.870 --> 11:13.860
Huh? My cat?

11:14.140 --> 11:19.050
Yeah. I heard from Takada-kun 
that you have a really cute cat.

11:19.050 --> 11:21.110
I-I see.

11:21.110 --> 11:24.170
I'd really like to meet him!

11:24.590 --> 11:27.870
So can I come over to your place sometime?

11:27.870 --> 11:28.510
Eh?

11:28.510 --> 11:29.470
S-Sure!

11:29.470 --> 11:30.270
What?!

11:30.710 --> 11:32.590
That's not fair, Adachi-san!

11:32.590 --> 11:36.190
I've never been to Nishimura-san's house!

11:36.190 --> 11:37.550
Huh? You haven't?

11:37.550 --> 11:38.900
Nope!

11:38.900 --> 11:40.170
Me, neither.

11:40.460 --> 11:42.680
You're so lucky!

11:43.010 --> 11:45.790
I-In that case, why don't you all come?

11:45.790 --> 11:47.640
Yay!

11:51.060 --> 11:52.100
Okay.

11:52.940 --> 11:54.700
That should do it.

11:56.260 --> 11:59.780
<i>This is the first time Takada-kun 
and the others are coming over!</i>

11:59.780 --> 12:02.010
<i>I need to make sure they're not disappointed!</i>

12:10.880 --> 12:13.280
Maybe this should go over here.

12:13.710 --> 12:16.710
Ah, but what if it went here instead?

12:21.290 --> 12:22.740
I'm home!

12:24.000 --> 12:26.350
W-Welcome home, Dad!

12:26.350 --> 12:28.220
What's gotten into you, Akane?

12:28.220 --> 12:30.060
Cleaning the house this late...

12:30.060 --> 12:31.860
Um...

12:31.860 --> 12:33.920
I-It's nothing.

12:33.920 --> 12:35.580
I just felt like it.

12:37.520 --> 12:40.770
I was just going to tidy up a bit,

12:40.770 --> 12:43.370
but then I started noticing 
things here and there...

12:44.080 --> 12:45.370
Wait a minute.

12:45.810 --> 12:47.930
Do you have friends coming over?

12:49.230 --> 12:52.380
Um... yeah.

12:52.380 --> 12:54.260
Tomorrow, actually.

12:54.260 --> 12:55.370
So that's it.

12:55.370 --> 12:59.080
I-I still have a lot to do!

13:03.620 --> 13:04.800
Hmm...

13:05.820 --> 13:08.080
This outfit?

13:08.080 --> 13:09.070
Okay!

13:11.720 --> 13:13.890
Now I have to clean up again...

13:13.890 --> 13:17.070
Wh-What else do I need?

13:21.780 --> 13:23.060
Dad!

13:23.060 --> 13:26.120
Akane, dinner's not quite ready yet...

13:26.120 --> 13:27.410
Um...

13:27.410 --> 13:30.160
I thought your friends were 
coming over tomorrow.

13:30.680 --> 13:33.110
Well, I was just... making sure...

13:33.390 --> 13:36.130
It's fine. That looks great on you.

13:36.130 --> 13:37.710
R-Really?

13:37.710 --> 13:38.970
What a relief.

13:38.970 --> 13:40.870
M-More importantly, about tomorrow!

13:41.400 --> 13:43.760
I want to have snacks for everyone.

13:43.760 --> 13:46.130
Do you think there are any 
pastry shops still open?

13:46.130 --> 13:48.630
Y-You want to buy some <i>now</i>?!

13:48.920 --> 13:52.890
I-It can be at a station
within walking distance!

13:52.890 --> 13:56.370
When I went over to Umi-chan's,
 she served me cake...

13:56.750 --> 13:58.140
I-I get it.

13:58.370 --> 13:59.700
Give me a minute.

14:00.400 --> 14:02.900
That-There Shopping District

14:00.400 --> 14:02.900
<b>Megane Ichibangai</b>

14:02.900 --> 14:09.910
<b>Cheesecake</b>

14:02.900 --> 14:09.910
<b>Dark Chocolate Cake</b>

14:02.900 --> 14:09.910
<b>Shortcake</b>

14:03.100 --> 14:08.510
I think Takada-kun would like 
the dark chocolate cake.

14:08.510 --> 14:09.920
It has the word "dark" in it.

14:10.400 --> 14:13.750
For Umi-chan... the cheesecake?

14:13.750 --> 14:16.540
That's what she served when I came over.

14:16.540 --> 14:19.910
Oh, but would she want 
to try something different?

14:20.210 --> 14:21.900
And for Hino-kun...

14:24.190 --> 14:25.750
Sorry about this.

14:28.520 --> 14:30.340
Thanks, Dad.

14:30.340 --> 14:31.040
Sure.

14:33.310 --> 14:34.220
Ah!

14:34.490 --> 14:36.650
Do we have black tea at home?

14:36.650 --> 14:37.350
Eh?

14:38.160 --> 14:40.300
Barley tea won't do?

14:51.260 --> 14:55.340
<i>I hope Takada-kun and the others like it.</i>

15:02.340 --> 15:04.180
Onee-chan, good morning!

15:04.180 --> 15:05.080
Rise and shine!

15:05.370 --> 15:06.770
Onee-chan, it's morning!

15:06.770 --> 15:08.740
It's morning, Onee-chan!

15:08.740 --> 15:11.550
You're so loud, Taiyou. It's the weekend...

15:11.550 --> 15:14.040
What's got you so full of energy?

15:15.360 --> 15:16.850
Actually...

15:16.850 --> 15:19.920
I'm going over to Nishimura-san's at noon!

15:19.920 --> 15:22.660
It's my first time at her place!

15:23.090 --> 15:25.590
Sorry, Taiyou, not today.

15:26.840 --> 15:29.480
Akane-chan's feeling under the weather.

15:29.480 --> 15:31.180
It'll have to be another time.

15:34.450 --> 15:37.150
Akane, does it hurt anywhere?

15:37.150 --> 15:38.890
Need me to go get anything?

15:38.890 --> 15:41.450
No, I'm fine.

15:41.450 --> 15:42.660
I see.

15:43.130 --> 15:45.290
I'm sorry, Dad.

15:47.190 --> 15:50.330
I selfishly asked for so much...

15:51.700 --> 15:54.840
That hardly count as being selfish!

15:55.420 --> 15:58.310
You don't need to worry yourself about that.

15:58.310 --> 16:00.250
Just get some rest for now.

16:00.250 --> 16:02.700
Okay. Thanks...

16:09.970 --> 16:12.860
<i>I'm sure they're all feeling disappointed.</i>

16:18.070 --> 16:20.030
I'm sorry, Kuro.

16:20.550 --> 16:23.990
Everyone was supposed 
to come over to see you.

16:24.430 --> 16:27.850
But things fell through.

16:28.690 --> 16:32.440
Looks like I got a little too excited.

16:33.620 --> 16:34.810
<i>Um...</i>

16:34.810 --> 16:37.620
<i>I thought your friends were 
coming over tomorrow.</i>

16:40.470 --> 16:42.710
Friends coming over...

16:43.130 --> 16:44.850
That's all it was.

16:46.930 --> 16:49.200
How embarrassing.

16:49.200 --> 16:51.620
Getting so worked up by myself...

16:52.390 --> 16:55.830
Just when everyone else was 
looking forward to this...

16:57.610 --> 17:00.780
Today was supposed to be a wonderful day...

17:01.840 --> 17:07.180
I was going to have friends over
for the very first time...

17:07.930 --> 17:10.340
What do I do, Kuro?

17:10.340 --> 17:13.850
I got so excited, I bought 
enough cake for four people.

17:14.500 --> 17:17.130
I'll never be able to eat it all.

17:17.860 --> 17:19.590
I'll help you out, then,

17:21.270 --> 17:22.770
and eat some of that cake!

17:25.490 --> 17:28.520
You'd get tubby if you had it
all to yourself, y'know?

17:30.400 --> 17:32.580
Takada-kun...

17:43.060 --> 17:44.920
I came to pay you a visit.

17:46.520 --> 17:49.600
<i>I thought they weren't coming today.</i>

17:50.400 --> 17:51.560
<i>A dream...?</i>

17:51.990 --> 17:53.610
We're here, too.

17:54.000 --> 17:55.910
We all decided to come!

17:55.910 --> 17:58.640
Don't be so loud, you two!

17:58.640 --> 18:00.160
Oh, yeah. Sorry.

18:00.780 --> 18:03.140
Akane-chan, are you okay?

18:03.140 --> 18:06.060
We'll leave right after a little visit.

18:06.430 --> 18:10.350
<i>Everyone's... at my house?</i>

18:10.680 --> 18:13.170
<i>Is this a dream?</i>

18:13.510 --> 18:14.870
Akane-chan?

18:15.230 --> 18:21.490
This is the first time friends
have come to visit me when I'm sick.

18:21.490 --> 18:23.760
I'm so happy.

18:24.840 --> 18:26.230
Thank you.

18:26.620 --> 18:28.300
Akane-chan...

18:31.310 --> 18:33.610
<i>What a nice dream.</i>

18:36.380 --> 18:38.160
I think we should get going.

18:38.160 --> 18:39.890
Yeah, you're right.

18:45.090 --> 18:46.900
Here, Nishimura.

18:46.900 --> 18:49.520
Coupons for free fried rice 
from my parents' ramen shop.

18:49.520 --> 18:52.120
Come and try it after you get better!

18:49.650 --> 18:57.030
<b>Ramen Hino
Fried Rice Coupon</b>

18:52.580 --> 18:53.610
<i>Huh?</i>

18:53.610 --> 18:57.020
<i>Hino-kun's parents run a ramen shop?</i>

18:57.670 --> 18:58.950
<i>That's weird.</i>

18:58.950 --> 19:02.150
<i>This really must be a dream.</i>

19:03.080 --> 19:06.530
<i>I wish it would never end.</i>

19:06.870 --> 19:08.630
Bye, Nishimura-san.

19:09.190 --> 19:10.620
We'll be off now.

19:14.950 --> 19:16.120
Don't go.

19:16.120 --> 19:16.820
Huh?

19:18.700 --> 19:20.190
I'm so lonely.

19:21.180 --> 19:23.160
Please, Takada-kun.

19:23.590 --> 19:25.050
Stay with me.

19:55.030 --> 19:57.830
My fever's gone down.

20:02.020 --> 20:07.370
I feel like I had a really 
embarrassing dream.

20:25.570 --> 20:27.530
T-Takada-kun!

20:27.880 --> 20:29.860
Oh, Nishimura-san!

20:29.860 --> 20:30.610
Good morning!

20:30.610 --> 20:32.480
G-Good morning.

20:32.480 --> 20:34.340
So you're feeling better?

20:34.340 --> 20:35.390
Thank goodness!

20:35.390 --> 20:36.790
I'm sorry.

20:36.790 --> 20:39.230
We had plans for the weekend...

20:39.230 --> 20:41.210
Don't worry about it at all!

20:41.440 --> 20:44.280
I have a strange question to ask.

20:44.280 --> 20:48.120
Takada-kun, you came to visit me, right?

20:48.120 --> 20:48.850
Yeah!

20:49.240 --> 20:52.690
Ah, that dark chocolate cake was good!

20:52.690 --> 20:56.160
It had a cool, grown-up taste to it!

20:58.130 --> 20:59.220
What's the matter?

20:59.220 --> 21:00.750
Oh, nothing...

21:00.750 --> 21:03.090
Thanks so much for coming over.

21:03.980 --> 21:05.330
And well...

21:05.890 --> 21:12.570
When you came to visit, did I...
say anything weird to you?

21:17.160 --> 21:19.280
Um...

21:19.280 --> 21:20.840
Yeah, well...

21:21.640 --> 21:23.950
N-Never mind!

21:23.950 --> 21:25.850
I must have imagined it!

21:25.850 --> 21:27.670
O-Okay.

21:28.040 --> 21:29.770
O-Oh, yeah!

21:29.770 --> 21:31.820
Thanks for the fried rice coupons!

21:31.820 --> 21:32.560
Huh?

21:32.560 --> 21:34.380
You should thank Hino-kun!

21:34.790 --> 21:37.520
O-Oh, yeah, you're right.

21:37.820 --> 21:42.850
A-Anyway, I'm glad you're 
feeling better now.

21:43.710 --> 21:44.650
Yeah!

21:49.790 --> 21:51.120
<i>Takada-kun...</i>

21:51.630 --> 21:55.230
<i>I didn't think he'd be so 
vulnerable to a direct approach.</i>

21:55.230 --> 21:57.100
H-Hey!

21:57.100 --> 21:59.240
What's with those two?!

21:59.240 --> 22:01.160
Did something happen?!

22:01.160 --> 22:03.850
Hey, answer me!

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next time...</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
<b>The Swift Reaper Alliance, the Cursed Song and Christmas</b>
